          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: A witness observed, on Thursday, October 3, 2013 at 7:40 PM, two fixed bright points advancing silently in a symmetrical and uniform manner. The observation of two similar bright points, like stars, continuously crossing the sky in a straight line, clearly suggests a passage of two satellites. A check with the Calsky.com site shows the passage, at the same time on a trajectory corresponding to the observation, of the Chinese observation satellite triplet Yaogan17, launched on September 1, 2013. These satellites are known to reflect the sun only slightly (magnitude 5 to 6), but they could probably be oriented in such a way that they become brighter. A video of other Yaogan satellite series satellites can be seen here. This could explain why the witness sees 2 and not 3. The GEIPAN classifies this case as a \"B\" observation, very probable satellites Yaogan.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "d4dc9225e5ff9561cc91ab3708a827a99f9c50d464253a02ecc2ab83875dd7ac"
        }
